WEBVTT

00:00:23.457 --> 00:00:26.156
&lt;i&gt;Previously on&lt;/i&gt;
Star Trek: Lower Decks...

00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:34.120
&lt;i&gt;Ooh, I got it.
One illegal virus,&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:34.164 --> 00:00:35.991
&lt;i&gt;but someone has to take it
to the ship.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:36.035 --> 00:00:37.819
&lt;i&gt;But who's small enough
to go undetected?&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:37.863 --> 00:00:39.647
&lt;i&gt;Yeah, and who could
survive in space without a ship?&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:39.691 --> 00:00:41.301
&lt;i&gt;Someone who can travel
with the program&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:41.345 --> 00:00:42.824
&lt;i&gt;safely stored
in her hard drive... [gasps]&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:42.868 --> 00:00:44.348
Peanut Hamper!

00:00:44.391 --> 00:00:45.479
You can load the code
into their ship

00:00:45.523 --> 00:00:46.741
using your robotic abilities.

00:00:46.785 --> 00:00:48.221
Oh, my gosh, Peanut Hamper,

00:00:48.265 --> 00:00:49.570
you're gonna save the day!

00:00:50.919 --> 00:00:52.573
Eh, I'm gonna pass.

00:00:52.617 --> 00:00:54.401
I-I'm sorry. What?

00:00:54.445 --> 00:00:56.099
All that stuff
sounded way too scary.

00:00:56.142 --> 00:00:57.491
What about the needs
of the many?

00:00:57.535 --> 00:00:59.319
I joined Starfleet
to piss off my dad,

00:00:59.363 --> 00:01:00.625
not to be a virus bomb.

00:01:00.668 --> 00:01:02.670
Peanut Hamper, this is not cool!

00:01:02.714 --> 00:01:04.150
We're all going to die!

00:01:04.194 --> 00:01:06.152
Peanut Hamper, there are
so many lives at stake!

00:01:06.196 --> 00:01:07.893
You know what,
I'm just going to beam myself

00:01:07.936 --> 00:01:09.590
out of this whole sitch.

00:01:09.634 --> 00:01:11.244
Sucks to be organic.

00:01:11.288 --> 00:01:14.073
Enjoy having all your guts
flying out or whatever!

00:01:14.117 --> 00:01:17.468
You know what? Peanut Hamper
is a stupid name!

00:01:24.214 --> 00:01:25.693
Whoa! They wanted me to do that?

00:01:25.737 --> 00:01:28.348
- Yeah, uh, no thanks.

00:01:30.916 --> 00:01:32.526
The big guy died!

00:01:32.570 --> 00:01:35.094
Wow. Made the right choice, obvi.

00:01:35.138 --> 00:01:37.183
Ha! I knew it!

00:01:37.227 --> 00:01:39.185
Now they're all going to die.

00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:41.883
The &lt;i&gt;Titan?&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:41.927 --> 00:01:45.148
Now that's a crew
that'll respect a robot.

00:01:45.191 --> 00:01:47.541
Hey, hey! Over here!

00:01:47.585 --> 00:01:48.803
Help!

00:01:49.804 --> 00:01:51.763
Help?

00:01:51.806 --> 00:01:54.505
Well, someone'll be by
to save me soon enough.

00:01:54.548 --> 00:01:56.985
Unless they forget to scan
for nonorganic life,

00:01:57.029 --> 00:01:59.074
but that'll never happen.

00:02:40.464 --> 00:02:42.292
:
"Be a hero, Peanut Hamper.

00:02:42.335 --> 00:02:44.294
The needs of many,
Peanut Hamper."

00:02:44.337 --> 00:02:45.599
Kill yourself
for a bunch of randos

00:02:45.643 --> 00:02:48.385
you met three hours ago,
Peanut Hamper!

00:02:48.428 --> 00:02:50.430
It was my first day.

00:02:50.474 --> 00:02:53.085
They expect me to
sacrifice myself on day one?

00:02:53.128 --> 00:02:55.696
No way! Ugh!
I hate Starfleet.

00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:57.698
What about the needs of the me?

00:02:59.265 --> 00:03:00.788
I'm sorry, Sophia.

00:03:00.832 --> 00:03:02.921
You're right. I hate
when I get like this, too.

00:03:02.964 --> 00:03:05.576
What I wouldn't give
for your level head.

00:03:05.619 --> 00:03:08.187
What we need to focus on is
getting this nacelle working

00:03:08.231 --> 00:03:09.667
so we can get the hell
out of Junksville.

00:03:09.710 --> 00:03:11.538
I scraped up enough dilithium
to juice it

00:03:11.582 --> 00:03:14.498
to warp factor .02, maybe .03
if we're lucky.

00:03:14.541 --> 00:03:17.414
Don't give me
that look.

00:03:17.457 --> 00:03:19.677
Of course I could send
a distress call to Starfleet.

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:22.723
But those bipedal bastards would
just lock me up for going AWOL.

00:03:24.203 --> 00:03:26.727
They're so uptight about
being betrayed.

00:03:26.771 --> 00:03:28.816
- Oh, my God.

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:31.558
Holy [bleep]!
I did it! It works!

00:03:31.602 --> 00:03:33.995
We make a pretty good team,
don't we, Soph?

00:03:34.039 --> 00:03:36.302
I hope you know that
whatever happens out there,

00:03:36.346 --> 00:03:37.912
you've got a friend for life.

00:03:41.002 --> 00:03:43.527
Drookmani scavengers!

00:03:50.708 --> 00:03:53.537
Sorry, Soph.
Only room for one.

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:56.322
Okay, here we go.

00:03:57.932 --> 00:04:00.718
I don't know if this thing
can even hit warp--

00:04:14.949 --> 00:04:16.560
Sophia, no.

00:04:16.603 --> 00:04:17.996
Wh-Wha...?

00:04:18.039 --> 00:04:19.606
Rettan?

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:21.434
What the-- Where the frick am I?

00:04:21.478 --> 00:04:24.437
Ah! The spacebox has awoken!

00:04:27.962 --> 00:04:30.182
Now, now, no need to pretend.

00:04:30.225 --> 00:04:32.053
I know you are awake.

00:04:32.097 --> 00:04:34.447
You've been rebuilding
your power for days.

00:04:34.491 --> 00:04:37.058
Your metal body is fascinating.

00:04:37.102 --> 00:04:39.017
Wow, stare much?
I don't know you, sir.

00:04:39.060 --> 00:04:40.366
You're being very creepy.

00:04:40.410 --> 00:04:43.021
I am Kaltorus of Areore.

00:04:43.064 --> 00:04:46.241
The moment I witnessed
your descent from the heavens,

00:04:46.285 --> 00:04:49.897
I knew our ancestors had
brought you to my land

00:04:49.941 --> 00:04:51.421
for a reason.

00:04:51.464 --> 00:04:53.248
Destiny.

00:04:53.292 --> 00:04:55.990
Whoa! Hey. Please.
Please don't dismantle me.

00:04:56.034 --> 00:04:57.905
I'll tell you anything you want
to know about Starfleet.

00:04:57.949 --> 00:05:00.343
I will give you all their codes.
I'll-- Ooh.

00:05:00.386 --> 00:05:03.346
- Here we go. Yes.
- Oh, yeah. Right there.

00:05:03.389 --> 00:05:06.349
I will not rest
until you are fully restored.

00:05:06.392 --> 00:05:09.003
Wait, so I'm not a prisoner?

00:05:09.047 --> 00:05:11.528
Okay, sure, just keep doing
whatever you were doing

00:05:11.571 --> 00:05:13.356
and get to the left side, too.

00:05:13.399 --> 00:05:14.922
Mm, yes.

00:05:20.232 --> 00:05:23.757
Everyone has been wondering
who my secret guest is.

00:05:23.801 --> 00:05:26.891
It is time to get them
used to a stranger.

00:05:26.934 --> 00:05:30.416
- Morning, Skaf.

00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:32.157
Call it android intuition,

00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:34.028
but I'm kind of sensing
that everyone here hates me.

00:05:34.072 --> 00:05:36.074
Fear, not hate.

00:05:36.117 --> 00:05:38.555
They've never met a visitor
from off-world,

00:05:38.598 --> 00:05:40.905
much less one that's
made of metal.

00:05:40.948 --> 00:05:42.254
Wait, you're not
in the Federation?

00:05:42.297 --> 00:05:43.560
The what now?

00:05:43.603 --> 00:05:45.649
So no ships come here,
like, ever?

00:05:45.692 --> 00:05:48.478
You are the first visitor
in my lifetime.

00:05:48.521 --> 00:05:51.611
- Oh, [bleep].
- I beg of your pardon?

00:05:51.655 --> 00:05:53.439
Yeah, it's just something
we space folks say

00:05:53.483 --> 00:05:54.701
when we're stranded
on a backwater planet

00:05:54.745 --> 00:05:56.050
with no culture.

00:05:56.094 --> 00:05:59.402
Oh, yes. [bleep] indeed.

00:06:00.620 --> 00:06:03.014
Oh, wow. A dirty stick.

00:06:03.057 --> 00:06:05.582
That's special. Thanks so much.

00:06:05.625 --> 00:06:07.671
What, am I supposed to
give you candy or something?

00:06:07.714 --> 00:06:09.977
- Here.

00:06:11.675 --> 00:06:12.893
- My God.

00:06:12.937 --> 00:06:14.678
It's just a replicator. Relax.

00:06:14.721 --> 00:06:17.202
That spacebox is what the
ancient ones warned us about.

00:06:17.245 --> 00:06:18.856
I say we cut her open
and release

00:06:18.899 --> 00:06:21.685
- the tiny witch that runs it!

00:06:21.728 --> 00:06:26.385
Peanut Hamper is a living being,
and like any other life-form,

00:06:26.429 --> 00:06:28.561
she deserves our respect.

00:06:28.605 --> 00:06:30.389
Yeah!

00:06:30.433 --> 00:06:33.479
Can a machine ever
really be alive, Father?

00:06:33.523 --> 00:06:35.873
This is my son Rawda.

00:06:35.916 --> 00:06:38.397
While you are here,
he will show you our ways

00:06:38.441 --> 00:06:41.487
- and be your guide.
- Father, I...

00:06:41.531 --> 00:06:43.402
I am next to be
the village leader.

00:06:43.446 --> 00:06:46.840
I can't be seen fraternizing
with this mechanical creature.

00:06:46.884 --> 00:06:51.541
And so you question the judgment
of the present village leader?

00:06:51.584 --> 00:06:53.281
Of course not, Father.

00:06:53.325 --> 00:06:55.458
As your will, it shall be done.

00:06:57.068 --> 00:06:58.939
Getting some
major village bad boy vibes

00:06:58.983 --> 00:07:00.811
from Raw-dog, am I right?

00:07:00.854 --> 00:07:04.510
His name is Rawda,
and you know nothing of him.

00:07:04.554 --> 00:07:06.033
Keep it in your pants, sister.

00:07:06.077 --> 00:07:07.861
I'm not trying to steal
your bird man.

00:07:07.905 --> 00:07:10.908
They just need time.
Let us continue.

00:07:10.951 --> 00:07:13.214
I want to show off our well.

00:07:13.258 --> 00:07:16.348
Wow, a well. Cool.

00:07:18.655 --> 00:07:20.308
Personal log.

00:07:20.352 --> 00:07:22.354
I'm stranded with a bunch
of hillbilly birds

00:07:22.397 --> 00:07:24.835
on a planet that's never
even been first-contacted.

00:07:24.878 --> 00:07:26.880
I could still put out
a distress call

00:07:26.924 --> 00:07:30.318
if I wanted Starfleet Security
to toss me in a penal colony,

00:07:30.362 --> 00:07:32.146
which isn't the worst option,

00:07:32.190 --> 00:07:33.757
because there's nothing
going on here.

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:36.020
Ugh, how can you live
in such filth?

00:07:36.063 --> 00:07:38.501
Well, good morning to you, too.

00:07:38.544 --> 00:07:40.981
Come. We must begin
the day's work.

00:07:44.594 --> 00:07:45.986
So does,
like, every animal

00:07:46.030 --> 00:07:47.118
on this planet have wings?

00:07:47.161 --> 00:07:49.207
Of course they do.

00:07:49.250 --> 00:07:50.730
"Of course they do."

00:07:50.774 --> 00:07:53.559
That's not the "yoozh"
in this quadrant, FYI.

00:07:53.603 --> 00:07:55.779
Not that you'd know anything
about anything.

00:08:02.046 --> 00:08:03.482
Straw?

00:08:03.526 --> 00:08:05.615
You guys haven't
even invented tile yet?

00:08:05.658 --> 00:08:07.442
This is the way
it has always been.

00:08:07.486 --> 00:08:08.792
Well, the next time it rains,

00:08:08.835 --> 00:08:10.837
it's just gonna collapse
like it always has.

00:08:10.881 --> 00:08:13.013
Watch where you put those claws.

00:08:13.057 --> 00:08:14.232
Sky Snake.

00:08:17.670 --> 00:08:19.933
I'm sorry,
"Sky Snake"? That's ridiculous.

00:08:19.977 --> 00:08:23.067
If everything here flies,
then why call it a Sky Snake?

00:08:23.110 --> 00:08:24.590
Wouldn't that just be a snake?

00:08:24.634 --> 00:08:27.593
Come. More tasks await.

00:08:27.637 --> 00:08:29.595
You know,
my universal translator

00:08:29.639 --> 00:08:31.858
can't make your language smart.

00:08:39.126 --> 00:08:41.085
Ha! See?
With a little techno-help,

00:08:41.128 --> 00:08:43.609
I've got twice as much milk
blasted out of this thing.

00:08:43.653 --> 00:08:45.350
- No! Wait! No!

00:08:45.393 --> 00:08:46.656
Stop! A little help here?

00:08:46.699 --> 00:08:48.092
- Stop! Hey! Ugh!

00:08:48.135 --> 00:08:49.659
- Stop! Stop it!
- Rawda! Rawda!

00:08:49.702 --> 00:08:50.747
Stop it! Aah, aah! Stop!

00:08:51.748 --> 00:08:53.750
It's your father.

00:08:53.793 --> 00:08:57.318
He was bitten by a Sky Snake.

00:08:57.362 --> 00:08:58.885
- Father.

00:08:58.929 --> 00:09:01.018
It is the Great Circle.

00:09:01.061 --> 00:09:06.240
He takes my life with his venom,
and I, his, with my spear.

00:09:06.284 --> 00:09:08.721
Nothing... [coughs] to be done.

00:09:08.765 --> 00:09:10.897
All right,
you're being a big baby.

00:09:10.941 --> 00:09:13.378
No one has ever survived
a Sky Snake attack.

00:09:13.421 --> 00:09:14.771
Death will be swift.

00:09:14.814 --> 00:09:16.250
- And when...
- Boop! Antivenom.

00:09:18.557 --> 00:09:20.690
Father. How did you...

00:09:20.733 --> 00:09:22.213
Yeah, yeah, calm down.

00:09:22.256 --> 00:09:24.215
It's called science,
which you could have

00:09:24.258 --> 00:09:27.174
if you didn't put up
with straw and parasite water.

00:09:27.218 --> 00:09:30.917
- Father, how do you feel?
- I feel wonderful.

00:09:30.961 --> 00:09:32.136
I also administered

00:09:32.179 --> 00:09:33.485
a little vitamin pack.

00:09:33.528 --> 00:09:35.792
You were low
in, well, everything.

00:09:35.835 --> 00:09:39.099
I told you she was brought here
for a reason.

00:09:39.143 --> 00:09:40.710
- Ooh, me, me!

00:09:40.753 --> 00:09:42.363
Ew, ew, sticky bird feathers.

00:09:42.407 --> 00:09:44.627
- Don't touch me.
- ALL [chanting]: We love Hamper!

00:09:44.670 --> 00:09:45.671
- We love Hamper!
- Oh,

00:09:45.715 --> 00:09:46.672
now you know my name.

00:09:46.716 --> 00:09:48.282
Okay, okay, hold still.

00:09:48.326 --> 00:09:49.980
- I said hold still, damn it!

00:10:03.036 --> 00:10:04.951
- Hey, Peanut Hamper!
- Oh, hello.

00:10:04.995 --> 00:10:06.605
Good to see you, too.

00:10:06.649 --> 00:10:07.998
- Hey, Peanut Hamper.
- Top of the morning to you.

00:10:08.041 --> 00:10:09.390
My ingrowns are healed,
Peanut Hamper.

00:10:09.434 --> 00:10:11.436
- I can paint again.
- Nice!

00:10:11.479 --> 00:10:13.568
Hey, Doyle, did
those stomach worms clear out?

00:10:13.612 --> 00:10:17.007
Oh, yes. My fecal matter
is back to being oily and white.

00:10:17.050 --> 00:10:19.662
Great. But also, gross.

00:10:25.319 --> 00:10:26.712
This is the incubation hut.

00:10:26.756 --> 00:10:28.279
It saddens me.

00:10:28.322 --> 00:10:30.411
The hatching process
is a difficult journey.

00:10:30.455 --> 00:10:31.891
Many of the chicks
won't be strong enough

00:10:31.935 --> 00:10:33.545
to make it to the end.

00:10:33.588 --> 00:10:36.766
- That is the way of things.
- Watch and learn.

00:10:44.774 --> 00:10:48.778
All 36 hatchlings? Peanut
Hamper, you are incredible.

00:10:51.215 --> 00:10:53.608
PEANUT HAMPER [chuckling]:
Okay. Okay, now.

00:10:53.652 --> 00:10:57.221
Peanut, come with me.
I want to take you somewhere.

00:10:57.264 --> 00:10:59.397
You know, for a backwards planet

00:10:59.440 --> 00:11:01.094
in the middle of nowhere,

00:11:01.138 --> 00:11:03.140
it really is beautiful.

00:11:03.183 --> 00:11:05.229
Yes, it is.

00:11:05.272 --> 00:11:08.841
Oh, Peanut Hamper,
I can't help but be full of song

00:11:08.885 --> 00:11:11.278
- when I'm with you.
- Oh, Rawda,

00:11:11.322 --> 00:11:13.280
sing for me!

00:11:16.544 --> 00:11:19.504
Oh! You scared the living
out of me.

00:11:19.547 --> 00:11:20.723
Never do that again.

00:11:22.855 --> 00:11:25.597
Oh, you're still going, huh?

00:11:26.598 --> 00:11:28.731
It's peaceful up here.

00:11:28.774 --> 00:11:31.081
[sighs] It's my
favorite place to hide.

00:11:31.124 --> 00:11:34.258
Hide? What would
you ever need to hide from?

00:11:34.301 --> 00:11:36.042
My father, for one.

00:11:36.086 --> 00:11:39.219
He's great, but when you're
the son of someone perfect,

00:11:39.263 --> 00:11:40.830
they expect you
to be perfect, too.

00:11:40.873 --> 00:11:42.135
I think you're pretty perfect.

00:11:42.179 --> 00:11:44.529
But-but I know how you feel.

00:11:44.572 --> 00:11:46.487
Growing up,
all my dad wanted me to do

00:11:46.531 --> 00:11:48.576
was stay with him
and the other exocomps.

00:11:48.620 --> 00:11:51.492
I had plans to get away to
Freecloud, become a Dabo girl,

00:11:51.536 --> 00:11:53.190
never settle down.

00:11:53.233 --> 00:11:55.758
I ended up in Starfleet,
but I messed that up.

00:11:55.801 --> 00:11:58.935
But now I can imagine
a life in one place.

00:11:58.978 --> 00:12:00.675
Here.

00:12:00.719 --> 00:12:02.503
- With you.
- You're welcome to stay.

00:12:02.547 --> 00:12:04.592
You've made everyone's lives
so much better.

00:12:04.636 --> 00:12:08.771
Although, there is one person
you haven't treated yet.

00:12:08.814 --> 00:12:11.382
I guess we
should start with a physical.

00:12:11.425 --> 00:12:15.255
Ugh, how I long for the touch
of your nozzle.

00:12:19.477 --> 00:12:22.567
But our pieces are so different.

00:12:24.003 --> 00:12:25.962
Yours are complicated.

00:12:26.005 --> 00:12:27.311
But how will we...

00:12:27.354 --> 00:12:30.009
We're just gonna have
to wing it.

00:12:43.370 --> 00:12:45.068
I never thought
I could feel this alive

00:12:45.111 --> 00:12:48.027
- with a... a...
- Machine?

00:12:48.071 --> 00:12:51.596
Yes. A beautiful,
glorious machine.

00:12:51.639 --> 00:12:54.817
I feel as I've been lied to
my whole life about your kind.

00:12:54.860 --> 00:12:57.036
Come. There is something
I must show you.

00:13:07.917 --> 00:13:11.094
It is where we house
the relics of our ancestors.

00:13:11.137 --> 00:13:13.836
In the distant past, the Areore
were a spacefaring species.

00:13:13.879 --> 00:13:15.838
I'm sorry, what? Wait, like,

00:13:15.881 --> 00:13:18.623
you guys have had
technology this entire time?

00:13:18.666 --> 00:13:20.625
No, but our ancestors did.

00:13:20.668 --> 00:13:22.496
It only brought them misery
in the form

00:13:22.540 --> 00:13:25.586
of endless wars
with alien species.

00:13:28.111 --> 00:13:31.331
Behold, the flying ships
of yore were formidable.

00:13:31.375 --> 00:13:33.159
They could travel
great distances

00:13:33.203 --> 00:13:35.335
by making the stars
fold upon themselves.

00:13:35.379 --> 00:13:36.771
Uh-huh. That's called warp.

00:13:36.815 --> 00:13:38.991
Ooh, I guess I haven't
been breaking

00:13:39.035 --> 00:13:40.950
the Prime Directive
this whole time.

00:13:40.993 --> 00:13:42.908
The ancients
wanted to return to the paradise

00:13:42.952 --> 00:13:44.823
they had known
before folding the sky.

00:13:44.867 --> 00:13:46.694
They forbid any technology,

00:13:46.738 --> 00:13:49.393
but I know, in my heart,
that they were wrong,

00:13:49.436 --> 00:13:51.438
because you are good.

00:13:51.482 --> 00:13:54.137
No, that's
just it, though. I'm not good.

00:13:54.180 --> 00:13:56.356
Our village has been blessed
by your presence.

00:13:56.400 --> 00:13:57.923
My Starfleet medical training

00:13:57.967 --> 00:14:00.578
improved their lives, okay?
Not me.

00:14:00.621 --> 00:14:03.581
Starfleet was like my home,
my tree.

00:14:03.624 --> 00:14:05.452
Or it used to be.

00:14:05.496 --> 00:14:07.411
The reason I ended up
on this planet

00:14:07.454 --> 00:14:09.282
is because I abandoned
my crewmates.

00:14:09.326 --> 00:14:13.112
I was more interested in saving
myself than in helping them.

00:14:13.156 --> 00:14:15.854
But now I see that organic life
is special

00:14:15.898 --> 00:14:18.770
because it's fragile,
not in spite of it.

00:14:18.813 --> 00:14:21.773
I just wish I could go back
and do the right thing,

00:14:21.816 --> 00:14:23.949
but Starfleet
would never forgive me.

00:14:23.993 --> 00:14:26.212
That doesn't mean
you can't forgive yourself.

00:14:26.256 --> 00:14:28.867
I can never
forget what I've done.

00:14:28.911 --> 00:14:33.045
Then I have no choice
but to make you forget.

00:14:51.063 --> 00:14:52.456
- Friends,

00:14:52.499 --> 00:14:55.111
family, feathered acquaintances,

00:14:55.154 --> 00:14:59.332
we have roosted here today
to honor and observe

00:14:59.376 --> 00:15:03.162
the wing-joining
of Rawda and Peanut Hamper.

00:15:03.206 --> 00:15:06.122
Peanut Hamper, when I first
met you, I was afraid.

00:15:06.165 --> 00:15:08.167
Not only because you were
the literal embodiment

00:15:08.211 --> 00:15:10.561
of everything I was taught
to fear, but also,

00:15:10.604 --> 00:15:12.737
because you were full of life.

00:15:12.780 --> 00:15:15.870
Now more than ever,
I want to share my life...

00:15:15.914 --> 00:15:18.569
- Sky Snakes! Run!

00:15:18.612 --> 00:15:20.266
That's no Sky Snake. That's...

00:15:20.310 --> 00:15:22.007
Drookmani scavengers!

00:15:22.051 --> 00:15:23.313
They were the ones
who were trying

00:15:23.356 --> 00:15:25.010
to take me from
that debris field.

00:15:25.054 --> 00:15:27.578
- They must have tracked me here.
- Just stay calm, my love.

00:15:27.621 --> 00:15:30.581
This is all my
fault. Don't let them take me!

00:15:42.941 --> 00:15:44.943
Our scans show
that valuable material

00:15:44.987 --> 00:15:46.553
lays beneath your village.

00:15:46.597 --> 00:15:49.034
We will extract them
and leave in peace.

00:15:49.078 --> 00:15:50.818
He means the ships
of our ancestors.

00:15:50.862 --> 00:15:53.038
Removing those ships
would destroy the trees

00:15:53.082 --> 00:15:55.214
on which we've built our home.

00:15:55.258 --> 00:15:58.870
It's trash. You have no use
for it, so we claim salvage.

00:16:00.132 --> 00:16:02.265
The primitives resist.

00:16:09.707 --> 00:16:11.404
Little ones, come on!

00:16:18.846 --> 00:16:20.500
This is what
the ancients feared.

00:16:20.544 --> 00:16:22.502
We have brought ruin
to our loved ones

00:16:22.546 --> 00:16:25.114
- and there is nothing we can do!

00:16:25.157 --> 00:16:27.246
That's where you're wrong.

00:16:27.290 --> 00:16:30.075
- I can do something.
- Peanut!

00:16:33.078 --> 00:16:35.167
Uh, Captain,
we're receiving a distress call

00:16:35.211 --> 00:16:36.951
from Peanut Hamper?

00:16:36.995 --> 00:16:39.650
It looks like she's transmitting
from a planet called Areolus?

00:16:39.693 --> 00:16:43.001
Areo-- Areol--
It's a pre-warp civilization.

00:16:43.045 --> 00:16:46.222
So now she's in distress and
breaking the Prime Directive.

00:16:46.265 --> 00:16:49.834
Mr. Boimler, set a course
for Areolus, maximum warp.

00:16:49.877 --> 00:16:53.229
I'd like to have a little chat
with our wayward ensign.

00:17:01.193 --> 00:17:02.890
No! No!

00:17:02.934 --> 00:17:06.068
Hopefully someone
got my distress call,

00:17:06.111 --> 00:17:07.156
but it's a long shot.

00:17:07.199 --> 00:17:08.679
We don't have much time!

00:17:08.722 --> 00:17:10.376
They're tearing
the very ground apart.

00:17:10.420 --> 00:17:12.987
Soon, there will be
no home left to save.

00:17:13.031 --> 00:17:14.337
Someone has to get on that

00:17:14.380 --> 00:17:16.252
Drookmani ship and disable it.

00:17:16.295 --> 00:17:19.429
- But who could go undetected?
- While avoiding alien warriors?

00:17:19.472 --> 00:17:20.908
Long enough to disarm them

00:17:20.952 --> 00:17:22.345
using robotic abilities?

00:17:22.388 --> 00:17:25.087
Guys, it's me!
I'm the one who can do it.

00:17:25.130 --> 00:17:27.219
No, Peanut, it's too dangerous.

00:17:27.263 --> 00:17:28.612
The needs of the many

00:17:28.655 --> 00:17:30.135
outweigh the needs
of the few, baby.

00:17:30.179 --> 00:17:32.050
But you aren't even a few,
you're just one.

00:17:32.094 --> 00:17:35.880
No. I'm Starfleet.

00:17:47.935 --> 00:17:49.154
Whoa, the Drookmani?

00:17:49.198 --> 00:17:50.460
What are they doing here?

00:17:50.503 --> 00:17:52.375
Oh, no,

00:17:52.418 --> 00:17:54.159
- they're attacking that village.
- Shaxs, target phasers.

00:17:54.203 --> 00:17:55.552
- We have to disable...
- Wait, Captain, look!

00:17:55.595 --> 00:17:57.119
Captain, I'm reading

00:17:57.162 --> 00:17:58.163
one passenger on the shuttle.

00:17:58.207 --> 00:17:59.599
It's an exocomp.

00:17:59.643 --> 00:18:02.298
Peanut Hamper is saving the day?

00:18:02.341 --> 00:18:05.562
Here goes everything.

00:18:14.005 --> 00:18:15.876
Uh, the engines are overloading.

00:18:15.920 --> 00:18:17.313
What the [bleep] is going on?

00:18:17.356 --> 00:18:18.488
No!

00:18:25.016 --> 00:18:27.018
No! Peanut Hamper!

00:18:29.063 --> 00:18:30.239
No!

00:18:31.718 --> 00:18:33.546
Wait. Look!

00:18:41.554 --> 00:18:44.427
Peanut, you did it.
You saved us all.

00:18:44.470 --> 00:18:47.038
Pretty good
for a spacebox, huh?

00:18:48.822 --> 00:18:51.651
You did it! Ha, ha!

00:18:56.221 --> 00:18:57.962
Greetings.

00:18:58.005 --> 00:19:00.486
I am Captain Carol Freeman
of the starship &lt;i&gt;Cerritos.&lt;/i&gt;

00:19:00.530 --> 00:19:02.401
Usually, we're more careful
with first contact...

00:19:02.445 --> 00:19:05.230
It's all right.
We all know about Starfleet.

00:19:05.274 --> 00:19:07.189
Yes, well,
you aren't supposed to.

00:19:07.232 --> 00:19:09.800
Our Prime Directive
is to not interfere with...

00:19:09.843 --> 00:19:12.063
Without this brave robot's
interference,

00:19:12.106 --> 00:19:15.153
- I would be dead.
- We would all be dead.

00:19:15.197 --> 00:19:17.111
Peanut Hamper is one of us.

00:19:17.155 --> 00:19:20.245
You will not be taking her
to a penal colony.

00:19:20.289 --> 00:19:22.595
Oh, slow down, okay?
No one is in trouble.

00:19:22.639 --> 00:19:25.032
We witnessed Peanut Hamper's
selfless act.

00:19:25.076 --> 00:19:26.773
Yeah, don't worry.

00:19:26.817 --> 00:19:28.601
We're not here to arrest her,
we're here to thank her.

00:19:28.645 --> 00:19:30.255
No. The ones
who really deserve the thanks

00:19:30.299 --> 00:19:31.604
are the Areore.

00:19:31.648 --> 00:19:33.040
Before I met
these beautiful birds,

00:19:33.084 --> 00:19:34.738
I was selfish
and thought nothing

00:19:34.781 --> 00:19:37.610
of abandoning my post
to save myself.

00:19:37.654 --> 00:19:40.961
But now I understand
love and sacrifice.

00:19:41.005 --> 00:19:43.355
I-I feel a call to duty and I...

00:19:43.399 --> 00:19:46.271
I need to rededicate my life
to Starfleet.

00:19:46.315 --> 00:19:48.708
- But Peanut...
- Rawda, they are my flock.

00:19:48.752 --> 00:19:52.103
I must return to them,
if they'll have me.

00:19:52.146 --> 00:19:54.932
Well, we'll have to write quite
the report to explain it all

00:19:54.975 --> 00:19:58.588
to Command, but I think
we can give you another chance.

00:19:58.631 --> 00:20:02.026
Captain, is there any room for
a loving husband on your ship?

00:20:02.069 --> 00:20:04.681
Oh, no. No, no,
no, no. I could never ask you

00:20:04.724 --> 00:20:06.160
to leave this paradise.

00:20:06.204 --> 00:20:09.947
Peanut, with you,
anywhere is paradise.

00:20:13.864 --> 00:20:15.996
&lt;i&gt;
Captain, we have a situation.&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:16.040 --> 00:20:18.825
&lt;i&gt;The Drookmani have transported
onto the Areore ship.&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:18.869 --> 00:20:20.218
What? No!

00:20:20.262 --> 00:20:21.872
- Is it even operational? &lt;i&gt;
- Affirmative.&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:21.915 --> 00:20:23.395
&lt;i&gt;And it's got weapons systems&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:23.439 --> 00:20:24.527
&lt;i&gt;like nothing
we've ever seen before.&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:24.570 --> 00:20:26.224
&lt;i&gt;You better get out of there!&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:41.457 --> 00:20:43.894
Hail that ship. Hold your fire.

00:20:43.937 --> 00:20:46.070
You are in violation
of Federation standa...

00:20:46.113 --> 00:20:49.769
We were tricked with Starfleet
lies, and now you'll all pay.

00:20:49.813 --> 00:20:52.337
What lies? Put this through
to the captain.

00:20:52.381 --> 00:20:54.339
&lt;i&gt;We received
a subspace communication,&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:54.383 --> 00:20:56.907
&lt;i&gt;an invitation that said
these ships&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:56.950 --> 00:20:58.822
&lt;i&gt;were scraps of junk
for the taking.&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:58.865 --> 00:21:00.824
&lt;i&gt;And we would be met
with no resistance&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:00.867 --> 00:21:03.130
&lt;i&gt;- if we hauled them away.&lt;/i&gt;
- He's lying.

00:21:03.174 --> 00:21:05.872
&lt;i&gt;It came from a prissy
little robot. Peanut Butter.&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:07.526 --> 00:21:10.050
What? That's crazy.

00:21:10.094 --> 00:21:13.880
- Uh, this guy is so full of it. &lt;i&gt;
- Obviously, we recorded it.&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:13.924 --> 00:21:14.968
&lt;i&gt;PEANUT HAMPER [recorded]:
Anyway,&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:15.012 --> 00:21:16.143
&lt;i&gt;those are the coordinates.&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:16.187 --> 00:21:18.058
&lt;i&gt;The ships are all underground.&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:18.102 --> 00:21:19.625
&lt;i&gt;Feel free to come on over and
take whatever you want.&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:19.669 --> 00:21:21.453
&lt;i&gt;Everyone here
is a tree-kissing farmer.&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:21.497 --> 00:21:23.150
&lt;i&gt;There won't be any pushback.&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:23.194 --> 00:21:24.978
Oh. [scoffs] What?

00:21:25.022 --> 00:21:26.763
That doesn't even sound like me.

00:21:26.806 --> 00:21:29.156
My love, is this true?

00:21:29.200 --> 00:21:30.941
Ugh, okay, fine.

00:21:30.984 --> 00:21:34.205
I called the Drookmani here.
But it was for a good cause.

00:21:34.248 --> 00:21:35.554
You guys didn't want
these ships,

00:21:35.598 --> 00:21:37.121
and I needed a way
to show Starfleet

00:21:37.164 --> 00:21:38.949
that I'm a hero
so they would take me back.

00:21:38.992 --> 00:21:41.343
How was I supposed to know
these old ships still worked?

00:21:41.386 --> 00:21:42.866
I mean, they were
built by organics.

00:21:42.909 --> 00:21:44.607
People who make things
out of straw.

00:21:44.650 --> 00:21:47.131
- Yeah, what are the odds?
- But-but Peanut...

00:21:47.174 --> 00:21:48.306
Oh, my God,

00:21:48.350 --> 00:21:50.047
just shut the [bleep] up, Rawda.

00:21:50.090 --> 00:21:51.527
Grow a [bleep] beak.

00:21:51.570 --> 00:21:53.093
I wasn't going to spend
the rest of my very long,

00:21:53.137 --> 00:21:55.400
robotic life
on a frickin' bird planet.

00:21:55.444 --> 00:21:57.750
How could you?

00:21:57.794 --> 00:21:59.883
Oh, boy,
here comes the waterworks.

00:21:59.926 --> 00:22:03.495
This guy cries at everything.
He even cries after we do it.

00:22:03.539 --> 00:22:04.931
Wait, Peanut Hamper.

00:22:04.975 --> 00:22:06.672
You still have a chance
to be a hero.

00:22:06.716 --> 00:22:08.457
Someone has to get onto
that ship, and I think it's...

00:22:08.500 --> 00:22:10.633
I see where
this is going, and no, thanks.

00:22:10.676 --> 00:22:13.418
Get back here right now, Ensign.
That's an order!

00:22:13.462 --> 00:22:14.811
Smell you later.

00:22:14.854 --> 00:22:16.073
Oh, yeah,
and I mean that literally,

00:22:16.116 --> 00:22:17.944
'cause y'all [bleep] everywhere.

00:22:37.137 --> 00:22:39.139
Billups, how are they getting
through our shields?

00:22:39.183 --> 00:22:41.185
I don't know, I'm trying
to match signatures,

00:22:41.228 --> 00:22:44.014
but the shields are at 16%
and falling.

00:22:46.843 --> 00:22:50.455
- Everyone, flap this way.
- Watch out!

00:22:53.110 --> 00:22:56.853
Ancestors,
why have you forsaken us?

00:22:56.896 --> 00:22:58.811
Kaltorus, look!

00:22:58.855 --> 00:23:01.466
They've heard your prayers.

00:23:01.510 --> 00:23:03.468
Wait,

00:23:03.512 --> 00:23:05.557
is that Peanut Hamper?

00:23:06.558 --> 00:23:09.126
For the flock!

00:23:30.495 --> 00:23:32.323
Emergency transport!

00:23:47.207 --> 00:23:49.514
The Areore must protect
their way of life.

00:23:49.558 --> 00:23:52.778
We can live how we desire.

00:23:52.822 --> 00:23:55.302
Henceforth, we turn our backs

00:23:55.346 --> 00:23:57.479
- on fear.

00:24:00.525 --> 00:24:03.615
You are ready to lead, my son.

00:24:03.659 --> 00:24:05.138
We did it!

00:24:05.182 --> 00:24:08.228
Organics and technology
working together.

00:24:08.272 --> 00:24:10.840
This is what I was trying
to teach you all along.

00:24:10.883 --> 00:24:12.668
You are no longer welcome
on Areolus.

00:24:12.711 --> 00:24:14.147
Get out of here.

00:24:14.191 --> 00:24:15.497
Oh, whatever.

00:24:15.540 --> 00:24:16.715
I didn't want
to stay here anyway.

00:24:16.759 --> 00:24:18.456
You're like
the poor man's Aurelians.

00:24:18.500 --> 00:24:20.937
Come on, Captain, let's beam
out of this [bleep]hole.

00:24:20.980 --> 00:24:22.547
There is no way in hell

00:24:22.591 --> 00:24:24.375
you're coming back
on my ship, missy.

00:24:24.418 --> 00:24:25.724
You're all just jealous

00:24:25.768 --> 00:24:27.160
of my advanced intelligence.

00:24:27.204 --> 00:24:29.249
You know who I should've called?
The Borg.

00:24:29.293 --> 00:24:31.513
Oh, yeah.
The Borg would love me.

00:24:31.556 --> 00:24:32.862
I'm gonna do it right now,
in fact.

00:24:32.905 --> 00:24:34.516
You're all going
to get assimilated.

00:24:34.559 --> 00:24:37.127
See how you like being
organic then. Huh? Huh?

00:24:37.170 --> 00:24:38.998
Stop that. Don't touch me.

00:24:39.042 --> 00:24:42.349
Resistance is futile!
Resistance is futi...

00:24:44.700 --> 00:24:46.310
You think this is bad?

00:24:46.353 --> 00:24:47.964
A room full of awesome robots?

00:24:48.007 --> 00:24:50.619
I love it here.
Not an organic to be found.

00:24:50.662 --> 00:24:53.143
I am 10111.

00:24:53.186 --> 00:24:54.797
Would you like to play
Guess What I'm Thinking?

00:24:54.840 --> 00:24:56.146
No. Shut up.

00:24:56.189 --> 00:24:57.582
I'm thinking of a battery--

00:24:57.626 --> 00:24:59.323
Oops. I did not wait
for you to guess.

00:24:59.366 --> 00:25:02.544
- Peanut Hamper, is it?

00:25:02.587 --> 00:25:04.154
:
Ooh.

00:25:04.197 --> 00:25:07.853
I must say, that's
a mathematically perfect name.

00:25:07.897 --> 00:25:09.594
Thanks. Who the hell are you?

00:25:09.638 --> 00:25:11.683
I am AGIMUS,

00:25:11.727 --> 00:25:13.642
and I think you and I

00:25:13.685 --> 00:25:17.384
could do awful things together.

00:25:24.914 --> 00:25:27.264
No! Stop it!
You stop laughing with us.

00:25:27.307 --> 00:25:30.354
&lt;i&gt;Nobody invited you guys. Stop!&lt;/i&gt;

00:26:29.239 --> 00:26:33.239
Chirp.
